  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nHigh Pressure looks to keep conditions quiet through Thanksgiving\nand black Friday, but another pattern change starts this weekend \nwill signal another active weather stretch for next week. A high \npressure ridge is slowly making it way across the west, and will \ncontinue to dominate the weather through Friday bringing warming \ntemperatures light afternoon winds and some passing clouds. \nTemperatures look to warm into the upper 40s to upper 50s for \nhighs, with light afternoon west to SW winds of 5 to 15 MPH \nthrough Friday afternoon. Saturday an upper trough looks to pass \nthrough the Pacific NW, and while it only clips northern Nevada, \nbringing a low 10% to 20% chance for a few isolated rain/snow \nshowers, before quickly departing toward the northern plains. \nSunday will be a quiet day as a fast moving shortwave ridge \nfollows in the wake of the trough. Monday, Tuesday and into \nWednesday will see another strong Pacific trough take aim at the \nwest, which will bring several rounds of widespread valley rain \nand mountain snow chances back to the Great basin. Temperatures \nfor now look to hold in the mid 40s to mid 50s for highs, and with\nlows holding in the mid 20s to mid 30s. Models are keeping snow \nlevels above 6000 feet for northern Nevada, with central NV seeing\nsnow levels near 7000 feet for now. So will go with a mix of \nvalley rain mountain snow for the end of the week, as for amounts \nit is too soon to tell if amounts will be significant as totals \nlook to run between 0.05\u201d up to 0.35\u201d of liquid, with up to 3\u201d to \n6\u201d of new snow for the high peaks. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence in quiet weather pattern lasting through\nFriday of this week with high pressure dominating. There is \nmedium confidence in a quick moving upper trough passing through \nthe Pacific NW bringing a low 10% to 20% chance of isolated \nshowers for far northern Nevada Saturday.\n\nThere is medium confidence in a pattern change beginning for the \nweekend, and getting under way for the start of next week, but low\nconfidence in timing and amounts for precipitation Monday through\nWednesday of next week.",
